## 1. What this is

A private site that shows every paper and project Victor has in flight, and what remains to be done on each one. Fourteen items today — six first-author papers, four co-authored papers, two latent spinoffs and two placeholders — and that count is a snapshot, not a ceiling: new papers get added as Victor starts them, so nothing in this brief or the build should assume a fixed total.

The core interaction is one thing: **select a block, see what is finished, what is left, and what Victor's next move is.** Everything else is supporting.

**Who uses it.** Victor, most days, to decide what to work on. Assaf, occasionally, read-only, to see where things stand without asking. Assaf said plainly he does not need it — it is Victor's tool that Assaf can also see. Build for Victor first.

## 2. What it is not

- **Not a task manager.** No due dates on everything, no notifications, no recurring items, no assignment workflow.
- **Not multi-user.** Two people, one of whom only reads.
- **Not a login system.** Access is handled entirely by Cloudflare Access in front of the site. Do not build a password field, a session, or a user table. See `DEPLOY_INSTRUCTIONS.md`.
- **Not a database app.** Content lives in one file in the repo and is edited by hand.

## 3. Stack

- **Vite + React + TypeScript**
- **Plain CSS** in one stylesheet using custom properties. No Tailwind, no component library, no CSS-in-JS.
- **KaTeX** — the only runtime dependency. Supplies both the Computer Modern typeface and inline maths rendering. See Section 7.
- **Vitest + Testing Library** for the handful of tests in Section 11.
- **No backend, no database, no API calls.** Everything renders from a static data file.
- **Deploy:** Cloudflare Pages, build command `npm run build`, output `dist`.

```
src/
  data/register.ts      ← real content, the only file edited routinely
  data/demo.ts          ← synthetic content for the public build (Section 12)
  types.ts
  App.tsx
  components/
    Header.tsx
    FilterBar.tsx
    BlockGrid.tsx
    BlockCard.tsx
    DetailPanel.tsx
    ProgressBar.tsx
    DebtList.tsx
    Tex.tsx             ← inline maths wrapper
  styles.css
```

**Why not a database.** The content changes a few times a week and is edited by the two people who own the repo. A file in git gives version history, diffs, rollback, and no infrastructure. If Assaf ever needs to write to it, that is the moment to add Cloudflare D1 and a Worker — not before.

## 4. Data model

Put this in `src/types.ts` exactly.

```ts
export type Role   = 'first' | 'co';
export type Kind   = 'chapter' | 'supporting' | 'latent' | 'placeholder';
export type Status = 'published' | 'in_review' | 'active' | 'blocked'
                   | 'not_started' | 'paused';
export type Court  = 'victor' | 'assaf' | 'collaborator' | 'external'
                   | 'compute' | 'none';

export interface Task {
  text: string;
  done: boolean;
  date?: string;        // ISO, when it was completed
}

export interface Action {
  text: string;
  owner: string;        // 'Victor', 'Victor → Paldor', 'Victor ↔ Assaf'
  leverage: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low';
  cost?: string;        // 'One email', 'About an hour', 'A few hours'
}

export type LinkKind = 'repo' | 'preprint' | 'doi' | 'data'
                     | 'figures' | 'manuscript' | 'slides' | 'notes';

export interface Link {
  kind: LinkKind;
  label: string;
  url: string;
  note?: string;        // 'Zenodo DOI, minted at acceptance'
}

export interface Debt {
  decision: string;     // 'MedWR domain fixed at 20–60°N'
  why: string;          // why it was taken, recorded NOW
  reconcile: string;    // what must be checked at synthesis
  affects: string[];    // other ids that must match or diverge knowingly
  resolved: boolean;
}

export interface Work {
  id: string;           // kebab-case slug of the paper's name — 'sst-circulation', 'beta-plane-paldor'
  role: Role;
  kind: Kind;
  title: string;
  short: string;        // 3–6 words, for the card
  objective?: string;   // 'Objective 1'
  venue?: string;       // 'Scientific Reports'
  status: Status;
  court: Court;
  courtLabel: string;   // 'Editor', 'Victor → Paldor'
  priority: 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4;
  updated: string;      // ISO, last REAL movement
  summary: string;      // one or two paragraphs
  tasks: Task[];        // done and outstanding in ONE array
  actions: Action[];    // Victor's next moves, ordered
  links: Link[];        // pointers OUT — see Section 10
  debt: Debt[];         // synthesis debt — see Section 10
  blockedBy?: string[];
  feeds?: string[];     // other ids
  note?: string;        // constraint, risk, or standing instruction
}
```

**One decision to get right:** completed and outstanding work live in the **same** `tasks` array, distinguished by the `done` boolean. Do not split them into two arrays. Progress is `tasks.filter(t => t.done).length / tasks.length`, and having them in one list keeps that honest — you cannot quietly drop a task by moving it between arrays.

**`updated` is the last real movement**, not the last file edit. It drives an ageing counter, and the ageing counter is the point of the whole site. If it gets bumped on every commit it becomes decoration.

